Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["\<\
Thermodynamic inference from excursions: double quantum dot analysis\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"803750d5-ecaf-4ac3-a61a-339d038a56b4"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook is a companion to the paper \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Thermodynamic inference from excursions: theory and \
quantum dot experiment\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], by Guilherme Fiusa, Jann van \
der Meer, Tan Van Vu, Vivek Wadhia, Natalia Ares, Gabriel T. Landi, and Pedro \
E. Harunari. 
All calculations, statistical analysis, data, and plots were extracted \
directly from here.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.004455983957591*^9, 
  4.004456041210229*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ca7449fd-7cfa-49d5-9e59-\
bc25e4f196b6"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Setup (run once)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4d8dadb2-3b18-467b-9e5c-11fe5a74828e"],

Cell["\<\
Analysis notebook for the double-quantum-dot data: excursion statistics, \
detection of detailed-balance violation and thermodynamic bounds for 0.855 V \
/ 5549 (main text), and, for the Supplemental Material, -0.955 V / 6013 and \
0.705 V / 5515, where the fourth state is common enough to be resolved in the \
signal histogram. Evaluate the Setup section once, then any run section. \
Requirements: Mathematica 14 and the MaTeX package (plot labels). Data: for \
each run, the files \"PCA--float64-(n,).dat\" and \"time-s-float64-(n,).dat\" \
(raw float64), in the folder structure set by dataRoot below.

Conventions. States 1 = (00), 2 = (10), 3 = (01), 4 = (02) at negative bias \
and (20) at positive bias; (11) is reached only virtually (cotunneling). Rate \
matrices are W[[to, from]]. 
Region A = {3}: the right dot holds exactly one electron. A counting \
observable for the edge x -> y counts +1 for x -> y and -1 for y -> x; q is \
its net value over one excursion out of A.

Pipeline: 
(i) States are assigned from the PCA trace: a three-level Gaussian mixture \
for states 1, 2, 3, plus the rare level 4 beyond level 3; samples further \
than rMax standard deviations from every level are dropped (transit), visits \
shorter than minVisit samples are dropped (state 4 kept at any length) and \
repeats merged. With useSingleModel = True (Settings), the levels and widths \
are instead those of the display fit (a Gaussian per level plus mid-jump \
components, emFitDetector), each sample goes to the nearest level with no \
transit cut (assignFromFit), and the emulated records of the benchmark are \
assigned the same way. 
(ii) Excursions out of A = {3} and their outcomes q. 
(iii) Estimators ln P(+1)/P(-1) and sigma_exc = K (P(+1) - P(-1)) ln \
P(+1)/P(-1), with rigorous one-sided lower limits (Clopper-Pearson, Garwood) \
or bootstrap intervals. 
(iv) Benchmark: the naive rate matrix from the recorded jumps (counts over \
dwell times), with a Poisson band when a reverse edge is rare.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0044560612076263`*^9, 
  4.004456099138994*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"79a8c5c6-d428-4fe5-8724-\
7a61cc5ddd6f"],

